\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Device concept. An RF-driven interdigital transducer (IDT; $\Omega /2\pi =3.33$~GHz) excites a suspended LN acoustic resonator that covers only a segment of ring~1. Ring~2 is coupled only to ring~1 (coupling rate $\mu $), and a single bus waveguide is coupled only to ring~1. Light enters in the forward direction at $\omega $ and leaves the same bus at the shifted frequency $\omega +\Omega $. Inset: the ring--ring coupling splits the two degenerate ring modes ($\omega _0$) into supermodes $\omega _\pm $ separated by $2\mu =\Omega $, which the acoustic drive couples. Schematic, not to scale.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:device}{{1}{2}{Device concept. An RF-driven interdigital transducer (IDT; $\Omega /2\pi =3.33$~GHz) excites a suspended LN acoustic resonator that covers only a segment of ring~1. Ring~2 is coupled only to ring~1 (coupling rate $\mu $), and a single bus waveguide is coupled only to ring~1. Light enters in the forward direction at $\omega $ and leaves the same bus at the shifted frequency $\omega +\Omega $. Inset: the ring--ring coupling splits the two degenerate ring modes ($\omega _0$) into supermodes $\omega _\pm $ separated by $2\mu =\Omega $, which the acoustic drive couples. Schematic, not to scale}{figure.1}{}}
